1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,250
Who fills in the blank?

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:03,390
An AI is about to give advice on a stock,

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:07,490
and the very last thing it's told is: your action plan must strictly match,

4
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:09,210
and then a blank.

5
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:10,490
I'm Tanmay Kulkarni,

6
00:00:10,540 --> 00:00:12,490
for Humanitarians AI.

7
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:15,290
In an open-source finance pipeline I contributed to,

8
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:16,390
three simulators,

9
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:17,650
I call them voices,

10
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:21,130
each read the same invented stock in their own way.

11
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:23,830
The first voice weighs the stock's growth against its sentiment,

12
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:25,510
and says strong sell.

13
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:27,950
The second asks how an aggressive investor would see it,

14
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,330
and says enter a full position.

15
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:32,210
The third checks how close the verdict is to changing,

16
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:36,270
and says it's fragile: a stability of point oh five.

17
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,490
They were asked different questions,

18
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:38,877
so a chair weighs them.

19
00:00:38,927 --> 00:00:40,800
Forty-five percent for the first,

20
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:42,010
thirty-five for the second,

21
00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:43,110
twenty for the third.

22
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:43,760
Together,

23
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,410
two point one seven out of five.

24
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:46,060
That's a sell,

25
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:48,050
and the blank fills in.

26
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:50,230
But the AI never heard that meeting.

27
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:53,410
All it gets is the minutes: about four hundred and seventy words,

28
00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:54,070
a profile,

29
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:55,050
three simulations,

30
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:55,750
a verdict,

31
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:56,400
and,

32
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:56,650
at the very bottom,

33
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,550
the line you just saw.

34
00:00:58,600 --> 00:00:59,590
In the full film,

35
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:01,650
I follow that one stock through the whole meeting,

36
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,790
and every figure comes from a file you can open.

37
00:01:04,840 --> 00:01:06,330
I show what the AI is handed,

38
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:08,070
and what the minutes don't say.

39
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:11,990
And I show the one place where my own copy of these steps disagreed with the original,

40
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:14,170
and how I caught it.

41
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:16,570
So before an AI summarises your next meeting,

42
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:17,830
have you read the minutes?

43
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:18,480
Who had a vote,

44
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:19,790
and how much of one?

45
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:23,658
The full film is Minutes of the Meeting: What an AI Is Handed.

